\markup {
  \center-column {
    \line { \vspace #1 }
    \line { "I Duetto" }
    \column {
      \fill-line { "First Movement"}
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {M. 23. } Added 8th note duration to a to fill out measure
	to match Second Player's part.
      }
    }
    \line { \vspace #1 }
    \column {
      \fill-line { "Second Movement" }
      \wordwrap {
	\bold { M. 40. } The B natural carries to B an octave up.
      }
    }
  }
}
\markup {
  \center-column {
    \vspace #1 
    \line { "II Duetto" }
    \column {
      \fill-line { "Second Movement"}
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {M. 25. } Retained C\sharp from previous measure, same
	sequence appears a couple of bars later. Leaving it a C\natural
	was interesting, but probably not what was intended.
      }
    }
  }
}
\markup {
  \center-column {
    \line { \vspace #1 }
    \line { "III Duetto" }
    \column {
      \fill-line { "First Movement"}
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {M. 24. } Interpreted the 3 sixteenths as a tuplet to make
	up time. The figure is repeated elsewhere in both parts, and tuplets
	are often not indicated in the source. 
      }
      \vspace #0.5
      \wordwrap { 
        \bold {M. 45. } The F is sharp, following current key of G major and echoing Second Players
        part.
      }
      \vspace #0.5
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {M. 54. } Changed F to F sharp after listening. It seemed like
	the accidental was missing and listening confirmed it.
      }
      \vspace #0.5
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {M. 111. } Source had too many beats, changed F natural
	to quarter note.
      }
    }
  }
}
\markup {
  \center-column {
    \column {
      \vspace #1
      \fill-line { "Second Movement"}
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {M. 48. } Google translates the text "\"Grazioso, without repeats\"".
	Replaced wih "D.C." instruction.
      }
    }
  }
}
\markup {
  \center-column {
    \line { \vspace #1 }
    \line { "IV Duetto" }
    \column {
      \fill-line { "First Movement"}
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {M. 14. } Listening to score it seems the first note of measure is E Flat rather than
	F, echoing the phrase from measure 12 a major third down.
      }
      \vspace #0.5
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {MM. 35-37. } When listening to MIDI something was clearly wrong.
	At this point we've modulated to C major. Sounds much better
	when after I changed the E flats in these measures to E Naturals.
      }
      \vspace #0.5
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {M. 48. } Added missing eighth note rest. 
      }
      \vspace #0.5
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {M. 83. } Changed second F to F \natural, which seems to be intent.
      }
      \vspace #0.5
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {M. 118. } Quarter note rest doesn't match time required for
	repeat, changed to eighth note rest.
      }
      \vspace #1
      \fill-line { "Second Movement"}
      \wordwrap {
	It's unclear to me whether sections should be repeated.
      }
      \vspace #0.5
      \wordwrap {
	\bold { M. 29.} B \natural seems to be intended;
	source sounds awful unless B \natural is used.
      }
      \vspace #0.5
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {MM. 120. } Listening to MIDI output, the C\natural doesn't
	work, keeping C\sharp from previous measure.
      }
    }
  }
}
\markup {
  \center-column {
    \line { \vspace #1 }
    \line { "V Duetto" }
    \column {
      \fill-line { "First Movement"}
      \wordwrap {
	Replaced staccatissimo with staccato.
      }
      \vspace #0.5
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {M. 44. } Added dot to D on first beat to complete measure.
      }
      \vspace #1
      \fill-line { "Second Movement"}
      \wordwrap {
	Tried to simplify form. The two sections seem to
	flow together now but I may have altered the intent. }
      \vspace #0.5
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {M. 16.} Added dot to first quarter note to fill out measure.
      }
      \vspace #0.5
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {M. 27.} I try to avoid all unnecessary accidentals, and according
	to \italic {The Norton Manual of Music Notation}, an
	accidental is not required for the second B  \natural.
	But this seems too hide-bound for even me,
	so I put a courtesy accidental above the staff.
	(I find parenthesized courtesy accidentals so hard to
	read that they're even more annoying than regular courtesy accidentals).
      }
      \vspace #0.5
      \wordwrap {
	\bold {M. 45. } The B's following A \sharp s only make sense
	when they're natural, as in the following measure.
	After listening it's clear the last F is \natural.
      }
    }
  }
}
\markup
\center-column {
  \line { \vspace #1 }
  \line { "VI Duetto" }
  \column {
    \fill-line { "First Movement"}
    \wordwrap {
      Replaced staccatissimo with staccato.
    }
    \vspace #0.5
    \wordwrap {
      \bold {MM. 40,42. } Descending E and D are \natural.
    }
    \vspace #0.5
    \wordwrap {
      \bold {M. 46. } Made first pair of As thirty-second notes
      to make measure duration correct. I'm following rhythmic figure
      in M. 48.
    }
    \vspace #0.5
    \wordwrap {
      \bold {MM. 102, 104. } Descending A and G are \natural.
    }
    \vspace #1
    \fill-line { "Second Movement"}
    \wordwrap {
      Fine, etc, not marked. But I'm assuming same form in previous
      duets is intended here.
    }
  }
}
